MLOps - CI, CD, and CT
----------------------

In MLOps, you will commonly hear CI, CD, and CT. They automate different parts of the ML/software lifecycle.

1. CI — Continuous Integration

CI = Continuous Integration
---------------------------

It means automatically checking new code whenever a developer pushes changes.

===
Example:

Developer changes Python code
          ↓
       GitHub
          ↓
    CI Pipeline
          ↓
   ┌──────┴──────┐
   ↓             ↓
Run Tests     Check Code
   ↓             ↓
        PASS ✅

===

For your ML project, CI could automatically:

Check Python code
Install dependencies
Run unit tests
Test data-preprocessing code
Test prediction code

Main purpose:
👉 Make sure new code doesn't break the existing project.

====


2. CD — Continuous Delivery / Continuous Deployment

CD = Continuous Delivery or Continuous Deployment

CD takes the tested code/model and moves it toward production automatically.

===

For example:

CI passes ✅
    ↓
Build application
    ↓
Create Docker image
    ↓
Push to AWS
    ↓
Deploy
    ↓
Production

====

For your SageMaker project:

Code
 ↓
GitHub
 ↓
CI Tests ✅
 ↓
Build / Package
 ↓
S3 / ECR
 ↓
SageMaker
 ↓
Endpoint

There are two common meanings:

====

Continuous Delivery
→ Automatically prepares a release, but a person may approve the production deployment.

Continuous Deployment
→ Automatically deploys the release to production after successful checks.

Main purpose:
👉 Get tested software/model into production reliably.

===

3. CT — Continuous Training

CT = Continuous Training

This is particularly important in MLOps.

Normal software doesn't usually need to be retrained when new data arrives. ML models often do.

CT automatically re-trains the model when new or updated data becomes available.

Example:

New Data
   ↓
Data Validation
   ↓
Train Model
   ↓
Evaluate Model
   ↓
Is model better?
   ↓
   YES ✅
   ↓
Deploy New Model
   ↓
SageMaker Endpoint

For example, your insurance model was trained using historical insurance data.

Later, you get 10,000 new customer records.

CT can automatically:

Detect new data
Preprocess it
Retrain Random Forest
Evaluate the new model
Compare old vs new model
Deploy the new model if it performs better

====

| Term   | Full form                      | What it does              |
| ------ | ------------------------------ | ------------------------- |
| **CI** | Continuous Integration         | **Test the code**         |
| **CD** | Continuous Delivery/Deployment | **Deploy the code/model** |
| **CT** | Continuous Training            | **Retrain the ML model**  |


====

In your SageMaker project

A complete MLOps pipeline could look like:

          Developer
              ↓
           GitHub
              ↓
       ┌────── CI ──────┐
       │ Build + Tests  │
       └───────┬────────┘
               ↓
        ┌────── CD ──────┐
        │ Deploy Model   │
        └───────┬────────┘
                ↓
       SageMaker Endpoint
                ↓
           Predictions
                ↓
          New Data
                ↓
        ┌────── CT ──────┐
        │ Retrain Model  │
        └───────┬────────┘
                ↓
        Better Model?
          ↙          ↘
        YES           NO
         ↓             ↓
      Deploy       Keep Old

So the key difference is:

CI = Code → Test
CD = Tested Code/Model → Deploy
CT = New Data → Retrain Model

=====
